@startuml
title VibeGraph Use Case Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "User" as User
actor "Apple Music API" as AppleMusic
actor "Neo4j Graph DB" as Neo4j
actor "OpenAI API" as OpenAI

rectangle "VibeGraph" {
usecase "Connect Apple Music" as UC_Login
usecase "View Playlists" as UC_ListPlaylists
usecase "Select Playlists" as UC_SelectPlaylists
usecase "Load Playlist Tracks" as UC_ListTracks
usecase "Sync Music Data" as UC_SyncGraph
usecase "View Taste Analysis" as UC_AnalyzeTaste
usecase "Generate Recommendations" as UC_GraphRecommend
usecase "Generate Recommendation Reasons" as UC_Explain
usecase "Create Apple Music Playlist" as UC_CreatePlaylist
usecase "Retry Failed Action" as UC_Retry
}

User --> UC_Login
User --> UC_ListPlaylists
User --> UC_SelectPlaylists
User --> UC_SyncGraph
User --> UC_AnalyzeTaste
User --> UC_GraphRecommend
User --> UC_CreatePlaylist

UC_Login --> AppleMusic : authenticate
UC_ListPlaylists --> AppleMusic : load playlists
UC_ListTracks --> AppleMusic : load tracks
UC_CreatePlaylist --> AppleMusic : create playlist

UC_SyncGraph ..> UC_ListTracks : <<include>>
UC_GraphRecommend ..> UC_Explain : <<include>>

UC_SyncGraph --> Neo4j : save music graph
UC_AnalyzeTaste --> Neo4j : read artist/genre patterns
UC_GraphRecommend --> Neo4j : find recommendation paths

UC_Explain --> OpenAI : generate reasons

UC_Retry ..> UC_Login : <<extend>>
UC_Retry ..> UC_SyncGraph : <<extend>>
UC_Retry ..> UC_GraphRecommend : <<extend>>
UC_Retry ..> UC_CreatePlaylist : <<extend>>

note right of UC_SyncGraph
For the current prototype,
a fixed userId is used.
User-specific login can be added later.
end note

note bottom of UC_GraphRecommend
Recommendations are currently based on
frequently listened genres.
More graph algorithms can be added later.
end note

note bottom of UC_Retry
Retry is used when authentication,
graph synchronization, recommendation,
or playlist creation fails.
end note

@enduml
